 fingerprint notes that names function as variables. That said, I'd like to understand:\n- **Ilse** seems to speak the line \"There has never been a we\" most frequently — does she have a special role?\n- Is there a **central protagonist** (the unnamed \"he\" or \"she\"), or are all characters equally peripheral?\n- Should we define relationships between characters, or is their interchangeability intentional?\n\n### 3. **World Rules & History**\n\nGiven the Cold War espionage aesthetic:\n- What era is this set in? (Contemporary? 1970s–80s? Timeless/ambiguous?)\n- Are there specific organizations, agencies, or networks at play?\n- What is the significance of the **plane tree dead-drop** that \"had been there longer than the country\"?\n- Why does the wire stay silent for **exactly eleven minutes**?\n\n### 4. **Scope & Structure**\n\n- How many chapters are you envisioning for the full book?\n- Will the chapter titles follow a pattern (like Chapter 1: \"A Debt in Zürich\")?\n- Do you plan to introduce any variation or breakdown of the permutation technique as the book progresses?\n\n### 5. **Themes You Want to Highlight**\n\nBeyond debt, anonymity, and erasure, are there other thematic currents you want the bible to codify? For example:\n- Trust vs. isolation\n- Permanence vs. transience\n- Precision as both salvation and doom\n\n---\n\nPlease share whatever context you have for any of these areas — even partial answers help. If you're unsure about something, just let me know, and I'll draft a section based on what's implied by the text. Once I have your input, I'll synthesize everything into a structured **STORY_BIBLE document**.","cancelled":false,"resultMeta":{"findingsCreated":0,"statusAdvanced":false},"suggestedNext":["build-architecture"]}}
